Last weekend, I joined a volunteer activity to help build an HSBC Joy Space for Children in a less-developed city.

A foundation had already donated books, tables, chairs and a TV, and our job was to turn the room into a welcoming reading space. My main task was to label the books, sort them into different categories, and arrange them on the shelves. I felt just like a librarian! I think every book lover secretly dreams of being a librarian at least once, so this activity really made that dream come true for me.

Another highlight was making traditional paper carp, which is part of China's intangible cultural heritage. During the weekend event, many local children came to decorate their own carp by drawing details like the eyes and colorful patterns before taking them home. It was wonderful to see their creativity and excitement.

It was a meaningful experience, and I hope this new reading space will inspire many children to discover the joy of reading.
